A team card: members with roles and presence, a seat count and an invite-by-email form. A **block** composed from
Avatar, Badge, Button and Icon, as on the [Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui) - with the invite form wired up.

<%= embed AppicaUI::Blocks::TeamMembersPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
TeamMembers(seats: account.seats, used: members.size, action: invitations_path, list_id: "team") do
  TeamMemberList do
    members.each do |member|
      TeamMember(name: member.name, email: member.email, avatar: member.avatar_url, role: member.role.to_sym, online: member.online?)
    end
  end
  TeamInvite()
end
```

- The header shows the title and "4 of 5 seats used"; its **Invite** button focuses the email field.
- The invite form validates the address in the browser and posts `email` to `action:` (Turbo submits it). Reply
  with a Turbo Stream that appends the new row - the seat count follows the rows, and once every seat is taken the
  field and buttons disable ("All seats are taken").
- Without an `action:` the block runs a demo and adds the invited row itself, as in these previews.

```ruby
# app/controllers/invitations_controller.rb
def create
  invitation = Current.account.invitations.create!(email: params[:email])
  render turbo_stream: turbo_stream.append("team", AppicaUI::Blocks::TeamMember.new(name: invitation.email, email: invitation.email, role: :invited))
end
```

## Localization

The title, seat count, roles, presence labels and the form's placeholder, labels and messages are translated -
`team_members.locales.yml` next to the component (English, Czech, German and Arabic). Roles given as symbols
(`:owner`, `:admin`, `:editor`, `:viewer`, `:invited`) are translated; strings are shown as-is. Switch the
**Locale** display option to try it.

