## API reference

### TeamMembers

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `seats:` | `Integer` | - | Seats in the plan; shows the count and locks inviting when full. |
| `used:` | `Integer` | `0` | Seats taken when the page renders (then the controller counts the rows). |
| `title:` | `String` | translated | Heading ("Team members"). |
| `action:` / `method:` | `String` / `Symbol` | - / `:post` | Where the invite form posts. Without `action:` the block runs a demo. |
| `invite:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Show the header's Invite button. |
| `list_id:` | `String` | generated | Id of the member list - the Turbo Stream target. |

### Parts

| Part | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `TeamMemberList` | The `role="list"` of members. |
| `TeamMember(name:, email:, avatar:, role:, online:)` | A row: avatar (or initials) with a presence dot, name, email, role badge. |
| `TeamInvite(placeholder:, name: "email", label:)` | The email field and send button, under a divider. |

### Controller (`appica-ui--blocks--team-members`)

Emits `appica-ui--blocks--team-members:invite` with `{ email }` before sending - call `preventDefault()` to handle it yourself.

## Accessibility

- Members are a labelled list; presence dots carry "Online" / "Offline" labels.
- The email field is labelled ("Invite by email"), uses `type="email"`, and shows a translated validation message.
- The icon-only send button is labelled ("Send invite"); disabled controls stay visible but inert when the team is full.
